<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Data Table

A table of rows with sorting, filtering, pagination, column visibility, and row selection. `createDataTable` holds that state without a dependency, and `DataTable`, `DataTablePagination`, and `DataTableViewOptions` render it with the `Table`, `Checkbox`, `Button`, `NativeSelect`, and `DropdownMenu` components.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { DataTable, DataTablePagination, DataTableViewOptions, createDataTable, type DataTableColumn } from "#lib/components/ui/data-table/index.js";
	import { Input } from "#lib/components/ui/input/index.js";

	const { data } = $props();
	const columns: DataTableColumn<Payment>[] = [
		{ id: "status", header: "Status", accessor: "status" },
		{ id: "email", header: "Email", accessor: "email" },
		{ id: "amount", header: "Amount", accessor: "amount", align: "right" },
	];
	const table = createDataTable({ data: () => data.payments, columns, getRowId: (row) => row.id, enableRowSelection: true });
</script>

<Input placeholder="Filter emails..." oninput={(e) => table.setColumnFilter("email", e.currentTarget.value)} />
<DataTableViewOptions {table} />
<DataTable {table} />
<DataTablePagination {table} />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/data-table.json
```

## Columns

Each column has an `id` and a `header`. Set `accessor` to a row key or a function that reads the value; leave it out for display-only columns, such as actions. Columns with an accessor sort when their heading is clicked, cycling through ascending, descending, and unsorted, and are searched by the global filter. Set `sortable`, `searchable`, or `hideable` to `false` to turn those off, `align` to align the heading and cells, and `sortFn` or `filterFn` for a custom order or match.

Set `initialSort` in `createDataTable` to start sorted, `emptyText` on `DataTable` for the row shown when nothing matches, and `pageSizes` on `DataTablePagination` for the rows-per-page choices. In this demo the status column cannot be sorted or hidden, the amount is not searched, and the table starts sorted by amount, highest first.

<Demo section="columns" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	const columns: DataTableColumn<Payment>[] = [
		{ id: "status", header: "Status", accessor: "status", sortable: false, hideable: false },
		{ id: "email", header: "Email", accessor: "email" },
		{ id: "amount", header: "Amount", accessor: "amount", align: "right", searchable: false },
	];
	const table = createDataTable({ data: () => payments, columns, pageSize: 5, initialSort: { id: "amount", desc: true } });
</script>

<Input placeholder="Search..." value={table.globalFilter} oninput={(e) => table.setGlobalFilter(e.currentTarget.value)} />
<DataTableViewOptions {table} />
<DataTable {table} emptyText="No payments match your search." />
<DataTablePagination {table} pageSizes={[5, 15, 30]} />
```

## State

`createDataTable` takes `data` as a getter, so the table follows changes to the rows. Set `getRowId` so the selection survives sorting and data changes. The returned state has reactive fields you can read and set, such as `sort`, `globalFilter`, `columnFilters`, `pageIndex`, `pageSize`, `hiddenColumns`, and `selectedRows`, and derived lists, such as `filteredRows`, `pageRows`, `pageCount`, and `selectedRowList`. Its methods include `toggleSort`, `setGlobalFilter`, `setColumnFilter`, `setPage`, `setPageSize`, `setColumnVisible`, and `setRowSelected`.

## Cells

`DataTable` shows each value as text. Pass a `cell` snippet to render every cell yourself; it receives the `row`, the `column`, and the `value`, such as to show a status as a `Badge` or format an amount.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<DataTable {table}>
	{#snippet cell({ row, column, value })}
		{#if column.id === "amount"}
			{currency.format(Number(value))}
		{:else}
			{value}
		{/if}
	{/snippet}
</DataTable>
```

## Selection

Set `enableRowSelection` to add a checkbox column. The heading checkbox selects every row on the page and shows the mixed state when some are selected. Selected rows are highlighted, and `DataTablePagination` shows the count.

## Rows

Pass a `leading` snippet to add a cell at the start of every row, before the checkbox column, such as a drag handle; it receives the `row`. Set `leadingLabel` to name that column for screen readers. Pass `rowProps` to spread attributes and event handlers onto each row, such as `ondragover` to reorder rows or a `data-*` attribute for styling. Set `hideHeader` on a column to keep its heading for screen readers only, such as for an actions column.

<Demo section="rows" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	const columns: DataTableColumn<Payment>[] = [
		{ id: "email", header: "Email", accessor: "email", sortable: false },
		{ id: "actions", header: "Actions", hideable: false, hideHeader: true },
	];
	const table = createDataTable({ data: () => payments, columns, getRowId: (row) => row.id });

	/** Lets a row take the dragged row's place. */
	function getRowProps(row: DataTableRow<Payment>) {
		return { ondragover: (e: DragEvent) => handleDragOver(e, row.original.id) };
	}
</script>

<DataTable {table} leadingLabel="Reorder" rowProps={getRowProps}>
	{#snippet leading({ row })}
		<button type="button" draggable="true" aria-label="Drag to reorder" ondragstart={() => (draggingId = row.original.id)}>
			<GripVerticalIcon />
		</button>
	{/snippet}
</DataTable>
```

## Custom layout

The state is headless, so you can render it with the `Table` parts yourself instead of `DataTable`, such as for expandable rows. Use `DataTableColumnHeader` for a sortable heading in your own table.

<Demo section="custom" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Table>
	<TableHeader>
		<TableRow>
			{#each table.visibleColumns as column (column.id)}
				<TableHead><DataTableColumnHeader {table} {column} /></TableHead>
			{/each}
		</TableRow>
	</TableHeader>
	<TableBody>
		{#each table.pageRows as row (row.id)}
			<TableRow>
				{#each table.visibleColumns as column (column.id)}
					<TableCell>{table.getValue(row, column)}</TableCell>
				{/each}
			</TableRow>
		{/each}
	</TableBody>
</Table>
```

## API

`DataTable` extends the native `table` attributes and takes a `size` like `Table`. `DataTablePagination` extends the `div` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface DataTableColumn<T> {
	id: string;
	header: string;
	accessor?: keyof T | ((row: T) => unknown);
	sortable?: boolean;
	searchable?: boolean;
	hideable?: boolean;
	/** Keeps the heading for screen readers only, such as for an actions column */
	hideHeader?: boolean;
	align?: "left" | "center" | "right";
	sortFn?: (a: unknown, b: unknown) => number;
	filterFn?: (value: unknown, filter: string, row: T) => boolean;
}

interface DataTableOptions<T> {
	/** Returns the rows; a getter, so the table follows changes to them */
	data: () => T[];
	/** Column definitions, in display order */
	columns: DataTableColumn<T>[];
	/** Builds a stable id for a row; the index by default */
	getRowId?: (row: T, index: number) => string;
	/** Rows per page; defaults to `10` */
	pageSize?: number;
	/** Adds a checkbox column for selecting rows */
	enableRowSelection?: boolean;
	/** Starting sort */
	initialSort?: { id: string; desc: boolean };
}

interface Props<T> extends CompProps<"table"> {
	/** State from `createDataTable` */
	table: DataTableState<T>;
	/** Custom content for every cell; receives the row, column, and value */
	cell?: Snippet<[{ row: DataTableRow<T>; column: DataTableColumn<T>; value: unknown }]>;
	/** Content of an extra cell at the start of every row, before the checkbox column, such as a drag handle */
	leading?: Snippet<[{ row: DataTableRow<T> }]>;
	/** Heading of the `leading` column, kept for screen readers only, such as `Reorder` */
	leadingLabel?: string;
	/** Attributes and event handlers spread onto each row, such as drag handlers or data attributes */
	rowProps?: (row: DataTableRow<T>) => CompProps<"tr">;
	/** Text shown when no row matches; defaults to `No results.` */
	emptyText?: string;
	/** Row height, cell padding, and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}
```
